      "thin": false,
      "bodyText": "The UK government has paid almost twice as much to turn off windfarms in Scotland as it plans to spend on developing small modular nuclear reactors by the end of this decade, industry leaders have said.\nThe Nuclear Industry Association said ministers plan to invest £2.8 billion in the technology, compared with£5.1bn in so called constraint payments that have been made since 2021.\nSome £1.04bn was forked out in constraint payments this year up until the end of August. This is up from £648 min the same period last year.\nThe UK Government wants to open small modular reactors in Scotland, potentially at former nuclear sites such as Torness, Hunterston, and Dounreay. All of these sites already have grid transmission connections. But this has been blocked by the Scottish government which holds planning powers.\nSCOTSMAN.COM 'UK spends twice as much switching off windfarms as it does on nuclear reactors'",
