      "thin": false,
      "bodyText": "Herald letters\nUKRAINE fired more than 1,000 drones at Russia, and Russia retaliated using drones to attack Ukraine's southern city of Zaporizhzhia.\nThis made me think about the greenhouse gases created by wars all around the world. Why have politicians and those of a green disposition never told us the volume of emissions created by the Russian war against Ukraine, and the emissions that will be created in rebuilding the shattered infrastructure?\nThen, of course, there is mother nature, with her volcanoes, earthquakes, tsunamis, hurricanes and more. All emitting greenhouse gases which puny mankind can never control. No figure has been put on that either. What about music and sporting events? Do politicians really believe people will believe that buying an EV and a heat pump, and cycling to work and eating less meat, will save the planet?\nMeanwhile, most of the rest of the world is still harvesting and using fossil fuels to drive their economies.\nClark Cross, Linlithgow.",
